{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A wooden cube with edge length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> units (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5b7e9c297d5ee6dce5d1b385443c232bd4414b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />) is painted black all over. By slices parallel to its faces, the cube is cut into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba37f50c674bcbae995ed1d9dfd4beb5e53c765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> smaller cubes each of unit edge length. If the number of smaller cubes with just one face painted black is equal to the number of smaller cubes completely free of paint, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474000ee62572f9453156172e460d28474429dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 7 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 8 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"428\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that if we remove the outer layer of unit cubes from the entire cube, what remains is a smaller cube of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566aa684bcb55b4c157e26cb0a7faa94d391c3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, which contains all of the unpainted cubes and no others. This shows that there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1a89b0299cecd9ae215283272bf590aec449959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-2)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> unpainted cubes. Similarly, taking one face of the cube and removing the outer edge leaves a square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566aa684bcb55b4c157e26cb0a7faa94d391c3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> containing all of the cubes on that face with exactly one face painted. Making the same argument for the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> faces as well, we deduce that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2265273237ab8b79053ea708c94dda478bad6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(n-2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" /> cubes with only one face painted. \n</p><p>Accordingly, we require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a47fab4f4f807f90cf369b854a1ae657642570a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}(n-2)^3 = 6(n-2)^2 &amp;\\iff n-2 = 6 \\qquad \\text{(as } n &gt; 2\\text{, so } n-2 \\neq 0\\text{)} \\\\ &amp;\\iff n = \\boxed{\\text{(D)} \\ 8}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"504\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSM